{
  "id": "T-1751",
  "created_at": 1791543776.4336278,
  "parent": "T-1749",
  "role": "review",
  "tier": "sonnet",
  "complexity": 7,
  "title": "review: Two full gates ran at once in luna-inbox despite [gate].max_parallel = 1 (default): one on the gated_at lease path, one background run",
  "spec": "Evidence (luna-inbox, daemon pid 14714 on main 66d866c, 2026-10-09 11:58): two tests-green.sh processes started 2 s apart,\nwt/T-0679 (pid 48288) and wt/T-0681 (pid 48700), both children of the daemon; load average reached 411 and swap 18.8 of 19.4 GB.\nT-0679 pipeline gate keys: ['gate_attempts', 'gate_reds', 'gated_at', 'gated_at_lease'] gate_attempts=1; T-0681 pipeline gate keys: ['gate_attempts', 'gate_run_id', 'gate_started_at', 'gate_started_at_lease']. T-0679 had just finished a 52 min gate (its second attempt started at once); T-0681 started through the background gate\n(gate_run_id, gate_started_at). The two paths do not share the max_parallel count. luna-inbox pool.toml [gate] does not set\nmax_parallel, so the default 1 applies (orchestrator/gate.py:59).\nFind every place a gate subprocess starts (background gate start around daemon.py:1665, the gated_at lease / retry / re-gate path,\nthe merge-time tests-green run in merge.py if it runs a full gate) and make them all take a slot from one counter keyed by repo root\n(count live gate processes from leases plus the background registry). A gate that cannot get a slot waits for the next tick; never\nstart a second one. Tests (tests/test_gate_timeout.py or tests/test_daemon.py): test_retry_gate_respects_max_parallel,\ntest_background_and_lease_gates_share_slots, test_merge_tests_count_toward_gate_slots (if merge runs a full gate). Run:\nPYTHONPATH=tests uv run python -m unittest tests.test_daemon tests.test_gate_timeout. Commit on the task branch.",
  "inputs": [
    "T-1750"
  ],
  "acceptance": [
    "at most [gate].max_parallel gate processes per repo across all start paths",
    "the named tests pass",
    "tests.test_daemon and tests.test_gate_timeout pass"
  ],
  "scope": [
    "orchestrator/daemon.py",
    "orchestrator/gate.py",
    "orchestrator/merge.py",
    "tests/test_daemon.py",
    "tests/test_gate_timeout.py"
  ],
  "depends_on": [],
  "constraints": {
    "read_only": true,
    "budget_turns": 20,
    "timeout_s": 900
  },
  "status": "done",
  "assigned_to": "claude:A",
  "worktree": "/Users/k3ntaw/code/orchestrator/wt/T-1751",
  "codex_thread": null,
  "result": {
    "summary": "Every gate start path now takes a slot from one repo-wide counter. The daemon's background gate takes it in _start_gate and marks it held for its worker thread. merge and ship call run_gate directly, which waits for a slot. Live registry entries from other processes count toward the cap. I only read the diff and the gate.py imports. I did not run the tests, and merge.py is untouched in the diff.",
    "verdict": "approve",
    "comments": [
      {
        "path": "orchestrator/gate.py",
        "line": 220,
        "issue": "run_gate polls for a slot with no timeout or abort check. A stuck or stale registry entry, such as a long-lived unrelated process in the same pgid, would block merge and ship indefinitely while they may hold the merge lock. The Aborted mechanism is not consulted while waiting. Consider a bounded wait, or raise or hold so the caller retries on the next tick.",
        "severity": "med"
      },
      {
        "path": "tests/test_daemon.py",
        "line": 4153,
        "issue": "test_merge_tests_count_toward_gate_slots and the lease-path test call gate_runner.run_gate directly instead of going through merge.merge or ship. The claim that merge uses run_gate is therefore not covered by a test, and a later change in merge.py could drop the slot without failing a test. The tests also rely on sleeps (0.4 s) and the 0.05 s poll, which can make them flaky under load.",
        "severity": "low"
      },
      {
        "path": "orchestrator/gate.py",
        "line": 187,
        "issue": "The slot count treats PermissionError from killpg as a dead group in _group_alive, so a live gate owned by another user is not counted. This matches existing behavior but now affects the cap.",
        "severity": "low"
      }
    ],
    "packet_version": "8f3a2a608409",
